WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.200
Hi everybody, this is the Triple
P, Patricia Pie podcast.

00:08.200 --> 00:16.560
It has taken me many, many
moons, my friends, to get, it's
always hard, to get Patricia
into

00:16.560 --> 00:19.600
the studio here at the cottage.

00:19.600 --> 00:25.640
Many people have requested, we
play more of her songs, listen
to more of her story, and

00:25.640 --> 00:33.640
this is the only show where your
biggest fan gets to ask you
questions and play your music.

00:33.640 --> 00:34.640
And that's you?

00:34.640 --> 00:35.640
That's me.

00:35.640 --> 00:36.640
Oh, that's so sweet.

00:36.640 --> 00:38.640
Well, thank you for having me,
Mr. Curry.

00:38.640 --> 00:39.640
Yes.

00:39.640 --> 00:44.640
And you know why I never want to
do this, because I don't like to
look back.

00:44.640 --> 00:45.640
You know that.

00:45.640 --> 00:46.640
Yeah, but...

00:46.640 --> 00:50.640
You never hear me talk about it
or...

00:50.640 --> 00:51.640
No, never ever.

00:51.640 --> 00:52.640
No, I know.

00:52.640 --> 00:53.640
So how come...

00:53.640 --> 00:54.640
Always look ahead.

00:54.640 --> 00:56.640
So let's start right now.

00:56.640 --> 00:59.640
Why did you decide to do the
podcast?

00:59.640 --> 01:01.640
Because you're asking me.

01:01.640 --> 01:02.640
I know.

01:02.640 --> 01:04.640
Knife on the throat.

01:04.640 --> 01:07.640
That's all it took, is someone
to ask you?

01:07.640 --> 01:08.640
That's all?

01:08.640 --> 01:10.640
And you helped me in the
kitchen?

01:10.640 --> 01:11.640
Oh, okay.

01:11.640 --> 01:12.640
You did.

01:12.640 --> 01:13.640
I noticed.

01:13.640 --> 01:16.640
So can I start off with one of
my favorite songs that you've
done?

01:16.640 --> 01:18.640
Because, you know what?

01:18.640 --> 01:22.640
We have like four CDs, which is
probably 5% of all the music
you've made.

01:22.640 --> 01:23.640
Yes.

01:23.640 --> 01:24.640
It's just ridiculous.

01:24.640 --> 01:25.640
Yeah.

01:25.640 --> 01:27.640
How come you didn't look after
your shit, man?

01:27.640 --> 01:29.640
You should have at least kept
the CDs.

01:29.640 --> 01:31.640
See, that's why you're always
yelling at me.

01:31.640 --> 01:32.640
No, no, no.

01:32.640 --> 01:35.640
Because I made a lot of records.

01:35.640 --> 01:37.640
How many do you make?

01:37.640 --> 01:38.640
What's a lot?

01:38.640 --> 01:39.640
What's a lot?

01:39.640 --> 01:43.640
I think 75 to 100 records.

01:43.640 --> 01:45.640
Albums and CDs?

01:45.640 --> 01:46.640
No.

01:46.640 --> 01:50.640
And then say about 30 to 40
albums.

01:50.640 --> 01:51.640
No shit.

01:51.640 --> 01:53.640
So you have hundreds of songs?

01:53.640 --> 01:54.640
Yes.

01:54.640 --> 01:56.640
Maybe even like a thousand?

01:56.640 --> 02:01.640
Sometimes people play me
something and I don't even know
it's me or I know the song.

02:01.640 --> 02:02.640
I don't even know the song.

02:02.640 --> 02:03.640
I know.

02:03.640 --> 02:05.640
It's happened to me a couple of
times on the hit test.

02:05.640 --> 02:06.640
It's scary.

02:06.640 --> 02:13.640
If you meet people who know the
lyrics or sing along and I
think, shit, that's strange.

02:13.640 --> 02:18.640
And I will tell you later what
happens in my dreams because of
this.

02:18.640 --> 02:20.640
Is that the one with the
hookers?

02:20.640 --> 02:22.640
No.

02:22.640 --> 02:23.640
Okay.

02:23.640 --> 02:29.640
I'm going to start off with,
this is the genre I like that
you do best.

02:29.640 --> 02:37.640
Yeah, this is actually, I
started with this sort of music
because my daddy is a band
leader.

02:38.750 --> 06:08.750
[ Music ]

06:14.640 --> 06:17.640
You've got a little Ella there
at the end.

06:17.640 --> 06:19.640
Excuse me, put the mic in front
of your mouth.

06:19.640 --> 06:21.640
Ella was my favorite.

06:21.640 --> 06:26.640
So when I started to sing these
sort of songs, I was 15 years
old.

06:26.640 --> 06:34.640
15, and when I was 17, I went to
the nightclub where my dad's
band played.

06:34.640 --> 06:39.640
And in the weekend, I did some
songs in the nightclub.

06:40.640 --> 06:43.640
And how old were you, 15?

06:43.640 --> 06:44.640
I was 17 then.

06:44.640 --> 06:49.640
Actually too young, because
you're not allowed in the
nightclub.

06:49.640 --> 06:51.640
You weren't allowed to work
officially?

06:51.640 --> 06:52.640
No, no, no, no.

06:52.640 --> 06:56.640
So that was recorded in, I
think, 2001?

06:56.640 --> 07:00.640
Yeah, I did it again with my
dad's band.

07:00.640 --> 07:04.640
My dad is now, what is he, 78?

07:04.640 --> 07:06.640
No, he's 79.

07:06.640 --> 07:09.640
In 1978, he will be 79 this
year.

07:09.640 --> 07:14.640
And the band that you just
heard, they're all grandfathers.

07:14.640 --> 07:15.640
They're all his friends.

07:15.640 --> 07:17.640
Those guys are like half dead, I
remember that.

07:17.640 --> 07:20.640
This is sort of a hobby band,
and they still make beautiful
music.

07:20.640 --> 07:24.640
So you see that it doesn't
matter how old you are,

07:24.640 --> 07:27.640
you can always play music and
make music and it's lovely.

07:27.640 --> 07:32.640
So that's why I wanted to record
it, because it's wonderful.

07:32.640 --> 07:33.640
78, maybe.

07:33.640 --> 07:36.640
There was even one guy, 80.

07:36.640 --> 07:39.640
Was that the guy that couldn't
show up one day for recording,

07:39.640 --> 07:42.640
because they had...

07:42.640 --> 07:44.640
Yeah, how is that in English?

07:44.640 --> 07:45.640
Dottere.

07:45.640 --> 07:47.640
What is the word?

07:47.640 --> 07:50.640
They had to go to the hospital
to let his veins,

07:50.640 --> 07:52.640
like they cleaned the veins.

07:52.640 --> 07:53.640
I can't think of the word.

07:53.640 --> 07:54.640
Drew's heart, I don't know.

07:54.640 --> 07:56.640
Dutch is Dottere.

07:56.640 --> 07:58.640
Yeah, pump up the volume.

07:58.640 --> 08:00.640
Yeah, that was good though.

08:00.640 --> 08:03.640
They're so sweet if you see guys
playing.

08:03.640 --> 08:08.640
And that was on a Special
Collector's Edition EP.

08:08.640 --> 08:14.640
Actually, it's a very special
CD, because it only has four
songs on it.

08:14.640 --> 08:16.640
Hold on, I have it here in
iTunes.

08:16.640 --> 08:21.640
We recorded it actually,
especially for friends and
family,

08:21.640 --> 08:23.640
and just give it away to them.

08:23.640 --> 08:26.640
And a little known fact is that
on the CD,

08:26.640 --> 08:31.640
the title for Misty and a Foggy
Day have been reversed.

08:31.640 --> 08:33.640
Yes, that was wrong.

08:33.640 --> 08:37.640
Like 1500 CDs were the wrong
track titles.

08:37.640 --> 08:38.640
Exactly, yeah.

08:38.640 --> 08:40.640
I love that though, I love it.

08:40.640 --> 08:44.640
And that makes me think of the
time you sang with Tony Bennett.

08:44.640 --> 08:46.640
I don't have that recording
unfortunate.

08:46.640 --> 08:47.640
That was only on CD.

08:47.640 --> 08:49.640
No, we have it on tape, on
videotape.

08:49.640 --> 08:50.640
Your parents have that?

08:50.640 --> 08:51.640
No, we have it.

08:51.640 --> 08:52.640
We have it here?

08:52.640 --> 08:53.640
We have it too.

08:53.640 --> 08:54.640
What, on VHS or something?

08:54.640 --> 08:56.640
Probably, yeah, yeah.

08:56.640 --> 09:02.640
And it was a very famous program
in Holland that we had with Pim
Jakobs,

09:02.640 --> 09:05.640
one of the best jazz musicians.

09:05.640 --> 09:07.640
Yeah, lots of people know Pim
Jakobs and jazz.

09:07.640 --> 09:12.640
Yeah, and Rochie van Otlo, one
of the, what is it?

09:12.640 --> 09:13.640
Conductor.

09:13.640 --> 09:16.640
Conductors of beautiful big
band.

09:16.640 --> 09:18.640
Tony Bennett was in the show
that evening.

09:18.640 --> 09:24.640
And I had to sing a duet with
him, I remember.

09:24.640 --> 09:27.640
And the song that they chose, I
didn't like.

09:27.640 --> 09:29.640
Well, you did two songs, didn't
you do two songs?

09:29.640 --> 09:33.640
Yeah, I did two songs myself and
I had to sing a duet with Tony
Bennett.

09:33.640 --> 09:34.640
Yeah.

09:34.640 --> 09:36.640
And I hated that song.

09:36.640 --> 09:38.640
And didn't you tell him that?

09:38.640 --> 09:40.640
Yes, I said, I'm not going to
sing.

09:40.640 --> 09:42.640
Even if it's with you, I'm not
going to sing it.

09:42.640 --> 09:43.640
I hate it.

09:43.640 --> 09:44.640
You said that to Tony Bennett?

09:44.640 --> 09:45.640
Yeah.

09:45.640 --> 09:46.640
And what did you say?

09:46.640 --> 09:47.640
Yo.

09:47.640 --> 09:49.640
I said, no, I don't like it.

09:49.640 --> 09:50.640
And so we skipped it.

09:50.640 --> 09:51.640
We didn't do it.

09:51.640 --> 09:52.640
What song did you wind up doing?

09:52.640 --> 09:53.640
No, we did.

09:53.640 --> 09:57.640
At the end, we all sang a sort
of a song together.

09:57.640 --> 10:00.640
So you actually, you didn't
really sing a full duet with
Tony Bennett

10:00.640 --> 10:01.640
because you didn't like the
song?

10:01.640 --> 10:02.640
No.

10:02.640 --> 10:03.640
You don't even remember what
song it was?

10:03.640 --> 10:04.640
But he made a beautiful drawing
for me.

10:04.640 --> 10:05.640
That's true.

10:05.640 --> 10:06.640
And I still have it.

10:06.640 --> 10:07.640
You still have that?

10:07.640 --> 10:08.640
Yeah.

10:08.640 --> 10:10.640
He's quite a painter and a very
nice man.

10:10.640 --> 10:13.640
And he said to me, I heard that
you are actually a rock singer.

10:13.640 --> 10:16.640
He said, but don't ever do that
with your voice.

10:16.640 --> 10:17.640
This is what you should do.

10:17.640 --> 10:18.640
Yeah.

10:18.640 --> 10:19.640
I agree.

10:19.640 --> 10:20.640
Fuckin' A. Tony's right.

10:20.640 --> 10:22.640
But this music is wonderful.

10:22.640 --> 10:23.640
You can always sing it.

10:23.640 --> 10:26.640
You can always, even, it doesn't
matter how old you are.

10:26.640 --> 10:29.640
I hope this music will always
stay.

10:29.640 --> 10:31.640
Even with Frank Sinatra gone.

10:31.640 --> 10:32.640
Don't you think so?

10:32.640 --> 10:33.640
Oh yeah.

10:33.640 --> 10:34.640
And we really miss him.

10:34.640 --> 10:35.640
Don't we miss him?

10:35.640 --> 10:36.640
Absolutely.

10:36.640 --> 10:37.640
Fuckin' Lutely.

10:37.640 --> 10:40.640
Remember we saw him, one of his
last shows at the Meadowlands in
New Jersey?

10:40.640 --> 10:41.640
We did.

10:41.640 --> 10:42.640
Aren't we lucky?

10:42.640 --> 10:43.640
And it was canceled because he
felt ill.

10:43.640 --> 10:44.640
And we thought, oh shit, man.

10:44.640 --> 10:45.640
I was gonna fucking die.

10:45.640 --> 10:47.640
He was really bad at that time.

10:47.640 --> 10:49.640
He was on the ropes.

10:49.640 --> 10:50.640
I've seen him twice.

10:50.640 --> 10:51.640
I'm so happy.

10:51.640 --> 10:52.640
Yeah.

10:52.640 --> 10:56.640
I wish I'd seen the one at
Madison Square Garden that they
did the live recording.

10:56.640 --> 10:58.640
We've seen the one with Liza
Minnelli.

10:58.640 --> 11:00.640
We saw the one with Liza
Minnelli.

11:00.640 --> 11:01.640
Yeah.

11:01.640 --> 11:02.640
Yeah.

11:02.640 --> 11:03.640
That's right.

11:03.640 --> 11:04.640
Yeah.

11:04.640 --> 11:05.640
She was pretty sober.

11:05.640 --> 11:06.640
Yeah.

11:06.640 --> 11:07.640
She was pretty good actually.

11:07.640 --> 11:08.640
Yeah.

11:08.640 --> 11:09.640
But not anymore.

11:09.640 --> 11:11.640
Now she's, the voice you got,
ah, ah, ah, ah.

11:11.640 --> 11:13.640
When they do that, you know,
it's screwed.

11:13.640 --> 11:14.640
It's all over.

11:14.640 --> 11:15.640
It's screwed.

11:15.640 --> 11:16.640
Yeah.

11:16.640 --> 11:22.640
So what most people don't know
is that you don't sing.

11:22.640 --> 11:23.640
What?

11:23.640 --> 11:24.640
I mean, well, you don't sing.

11:24.640 --> 11:25.640
You don't sing around the house.

11:25.640 --> 11:26.640
No.

11:26.640 --> 11:27.640
I mean, once in a while maybe.

11:27.640 --> 11:28.640
No.

11:28.640 --> 11:29.640
I only sing for money.

11:29.640 --> 11:30.640
Exactly.

11:30.640 --> 11:33.640
Now, I think you should explain
this because it's very hard for
people to understand,

11:33.640 --> 11:34.640
even for me actually.

11:34.640 --> 11:37.640
I mean, if I could sing like
you, I would be all over the
place.

11:37.640 --> 11:39.640
I'd be like, yo.

11:39.640 --> 11:42.640
Well, there are all sorts of
performances.

11:42.640 --> 11:44.640
Performers, I think.

11:44.640 --> 11:45.640
Mm-hmm.

11:45.640 --> 11:56.640
And because my dad is a musician
that had to work really hard to
take care of his family.

11:56.640 --> 11:57.640
Mm-hmm.

11:57.640 --> 12:00.640
And so I didn't know what to
become and what to do.

12:00.640 --> 12:02.640
And I thought, oh, I'm going to
be a singer then.

12:02.640 --> 12:03.640
Yeah.

12:03.640 --> 12:08.640
So because we all got something
of music in our bodies.

12:08.640 --> 12:10.640
And so I started to sing.

12:10.640 --> 12:18.640
But in these days, you,
especially in clubs and in
hotels and everything,

12:18.640 --> 12:23.640
Germany and Belgium and Holland,
that was for the money.

12:23.640 --> 12:25.640
And that's how I started.

12:25.640 --> 12:26.640
And then when suddenly somebody…

12:26.640 --> 12:27.640
It was just a job.

12:27.640 --> 12:28.640
Yeah, it was a job.

12:28.640 --> 12:29.640
It was just my job.

12:29.640 --> 12:31.640
I didn't know what to do, what
kind of job.

12:31.640 --> 12:33.640
I thought, okay, then I'll do
it.

12:33.640 --> 12:34.640
But didn't you like it too?

12:34.640 --> 12:35.640
I loved it.

12:35.640 --> 12:37.640
There were moments that I really
enjoyed it.

12:37.640 --> 12:39.640
But there were a lot of moments
I hated it.

12:39.640 --> 12:40.640
Okay.

12:40.640 --> 12:42.640
Let's start with the enjoying
moments.

12:42.640 --> 12:48.640
Well, you know, if you have
wonderful audience and people
are really swinging along

12:48.640 --> 12:52.640
and looking at you like, wow,
you know, there was a great
evening

12:52.640 --> 12:54.640
because we enjoyed the music so
much.

12:54.640 --> 12:58.640
But you had also evenings that
people were very drunk,

12:58.640 --> 13:01.640
didn't hear anything, were
talking really loud.

13:01.640 --> 13:03.640
And that's horrible.

13:03.640 --> 13:06.640
Then sound comes out of your
mouth.

13:06.640 --> 13:07.640
But what do you like more?

13:07.640 --> 13:10.640
Do you like performing,
recording, writing?

13:10.640 --> 13:14.640
What I always liked was
recording.

13:14.640 --> 13:16.640
Right, that makes sense.

13:16.640 --> 13:19.640
So coming up with ideas, doing
backups.

13:19.640 --> 13:22.640
And I love that.

13:22.640 --> 13:25.640
Although they say I'm a very
good performer.

13:25.640 --> 13:27.640
I can really…

13:27.640 --> 13:29.640
How do you say that?

13:29.640 --> 13:31.640
You can rock the house, baby.

13:33.640 --> 13:35.640
Put on a show.

13:36.640 --> 13:39.640
I'm trying to think what we
should play next.

13:39.640 --> 13:42.640
I mean, we have four CDs, hold
on.

13:42.640 --> 13:46.640
Well, if we have to go through
the whole story, it takes very
long.

13:46.640 --> 13:47.640
Oh, no, we'll never be able to
do that.

13:47.640 --> 13:49.640
Well, maybe we'll do it in
parts.

13:49.640 --> 13:51.640
Yeah, we'll do another one
another time.

13:51.640 --> 13:52.640
But we need more music.

13:52.640 --> 13:53.640
I mean, I have…

13:53.640 --> 13:54.640
What do I have here?

13:54.640 --> 13:55.640
I have…

13:55.640 --> 13:56.640
But I have to tell them,
actually.

13:56.640 --> 13:57.640
At least 50 songs.

13:57.640 --> 13:59.640
So they know how it happened.

13:59.640 --> 14:03.640
When I was performing one of the
biggest night clubs in
Amsterdam,

14:03.640 --> 14:05.640
a very famous guy.

14:05.640 --> 14:07.640
I don't even know what the name
is,

14:07.640 --> 14:09.640
but I remember it was…

14:09.640 --> 14:11.640
That's how long ago it is.

14:11.640 --> 14:12.640
Wait a minute.

14:12.640 --> 14:13.640
This was…

14:13.640 --> 14:14.640
You were 16 at the time?

14:14.640 --> 14:15.640
No, no, no.

14:15.640 --> 14:16.640
I think 17.

14:16.640 --> 14:18.640
I played also the fiber phone.

14:18.640 --> 14:19.640
I keep…

14:19.640 --> 14:20.640
The what?

14:20.640 --> 14:21.640
The fiber phone.

14:21.640 --> 14:22.640
I have one of those in my
pocket.

14:22.640 --> 14:23.640
No, no, no, no.

14:23.640 --> 14:24.640
The fiber phone.

14:24.640 --> 14:25.640
Is that the word?

14:25.640 --> 14:26.640
Is that like a xylophone?

14:26.640 --> 14:28.640
We did George Shearing songs.

14:28.640 --> 14:30.640
I remember that.

14:30.640 --> 14:32.640
So I was singing and I was
playing.

14:32.640 --> 14:34.640
And we were playing in that
nightclub.

14:34.640 --> 14:40.640
And one of the biggest agents
from Europe,

14:40.640 --> 14:42.640
and especially Amsterdam was his
office,

14:42.640 --> 14:45.640
came in with a guy from the TV.

14:45.640 --> 14:47.640
And they saw me.

14:47.640 --> 14:48.640
I don't know why he…

14:48.640 --> 14:49.640
They came specially for me.

14:49.640 --> 14:50.640
Who was that?

14:50.640 --> 14:51.640
Lufa Reis?

14:51.640 --> 14:53.640
Yeah, Lufa Reis, who always…

14:53.640 --> 14:55.640
Yeah, he was a big supporter of
you.

14:55.640 --> 14:57.640
Yeah, I invited Shirley Bassey
these days.

14:57.640 --> 14:58.640
Oh, right.

14:58.640 --> 14:59.640
He was the impresario.

14:59.640 --> 15:00.640
Impressario.

15:00.640 --> 15:01.640
That's how you called it.

15:01.640 --> 15:04.640
And he came with a guy, Willem
Daus.

15:04.640 --> 15:05.640
Oh, Willem Daus, right?

15:05.640 --> 15:06.640
Yeah, Willem Daus.

15:06.640 --> 15:07.640
He was a talk show host.

15:07.640 --> 15:08.640
A talk show host.

15:08.640 --> 15:10.640
The Johnny Carson from Holland,
right?

15:10.640 --> 15:12.640
They came in and they saw me and
they said,

15:12.640 --> 15:14.640
Kit, do you have a record deal
yet?

15:14.640 --> 15:15.640
Really?

15:15.640 --> 15:17.640
No, I wasn't even thinking about
that.

15:17.640 --> 15:18.640
Really?

15:18.640 --> 15:20.640
And I said, well, we're going to
do that.

15:20.640 --> 15:23.640
We're going to go to one of the
record companies yet.

15:23.640 --> 15:24.640
You need a deal.

15:24.640 --> 15:25.640
So, and that's how it started.

15:25.640 --> 15:26.640
So they became your managers?

15:26.640 --> 15:27.640
Your pimps?

15:27.640 --> 15:28.640
Yeah, they became, yes.

15:28.640 --> 15:29.640
Your pimps?

15:29.640 --> 15:30.640
Yeah.

15:30.640 --> 15:35.640
And from that moment on, I was
actually famous.

15:35.640 --> 15:37.640
And it never stopped.

15:37.640 --> 15:38.640
Cool.

15:38.640 --> 15:40.640
That's why we escaped.

15:40.640 --> 15:43.640
No, they were sitting here in
the cottage.

